Name: scrollbarBackColor

Type: property

Syntax: set the scrollbarBackColor of <field> to {empty | <colorName> | <RGBColor>}

Summary:
Specifies the color of the track of a scrolling <field|field's>
scrollbars.

Associations: field

Introduced: 0.9.16

OS: mac, windows, linux

Platforms: desktop

Example:
set the scrollbarBackColor of field "Log" to "#202020"

Example:
set the scrollbarBackColor of field "Log" to "40,40,40"
set the scrollbarForeColor of field "Log" to "gray"

Example:
-- revert to the platform's native scrollbars
set the scrollbarBackColor of field "Log" to empty
set the scrollbarForeColor of field "Log" to empty

Value:
The <scrollbarBackColor> of a <field> is a <color> reference: a color
name, an <RGB> triplet, or an HTML-style color. If no color has been set
the <property> reports empty.

Description:
Use the <scrollbarBackColor> <property> to color the track of a
<field|field's> vertical and horizontal scrollbars. Use the
<scrollbarForeColor> <property> to color the thumb.

Native scrollbars cannot be recolored, so as soon as either the
<scrollbarBackColor> or the <scrollbarForeColor> of a <field> is set, the
engine draws that field's scrollbars itself: a flat track filled with the
<scrollbarBackColor> and a rounded thumb filled with the
<scrollbarForeColor>. The scrollbars keep the geometry of the native
theme, so clicking and dragging behave as before.

If only one of the two properties is set, the other part uses the
field's effective <backColor> (for the track) or <foreColor> (for the
thumb). Setting both properties to empty restores the native scrollbars.

The property applies to the scrollbars of a <field> only; it has no
effect on scrollbar <control|controls> or on <group|groups>.

References: field (object), color (glossary), property (glossary),
control (object), group (object), RGB (glossary),
scrollbarForeColor (property), scrollbarWidth (property),
hScrollbar (property), vScrollbar (property), backColor (property),
foreColor (property)

Tags: ui
